All three functions are implemented and `python3 test_impl.py` now prints `ALL PASS` (stress loop took 2.9s). I ran the suite after each function; the first two runs failed only on the next function not yet being implemented.

- **`encode`** in `rle.py`: emits each character followed by its run length, always with a count.
- **`decode`** in `rle.py`: reads each non-digit character followed by one or more digits and expands it.
- **`merge`** in `intervals.py`: sorts by start and merges intervals that overlap or touch, returning new lists.

The encoding is ambiguous if the input string itself contains digits (e.g. `"11"` encodes to `"12"`, which won't decode back). The docstrings and tests don't cover that case, so I left it.

`test_impl.py` is untouched. Nothing is committed, and the test run left an untracked `__pycache__/` directory.
